  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event conflicts with a rule in this repo, so I need you to decide how to handle it.\n\n**The problem.** ARCH-4 in `CLAUDE.md` says `OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos, and that \"renames and removals go through deprecation.\" Nothing in this repo shows whether either of them reads `channel`, and analytics-ingest seems the likelier of the two to use it. If either still does, deleting the field from `src/core/events.ts:16` would break a deployed consumer.\n\n**The order model isn't the problem.** `channel` isn't returned by `GET /orders/{id}` (`src/api/responses.ts`), so taking it out of the model doesn't touch ARCH-8. The only catch is that the model is what feeds the event (`events.ts:50`), so it can't go until the event no longer needs it.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Deprecate first (my recommendation).** Mark `OrderPlaced.channel` as `@deprecated` and keep publishing it, so consumers have a removal window. The order model keeps `channel` until the field is actually removed.\n2. **Remove it outright.** Only safe if you've confirmed that billing-service and analytics-ingest don't read `channel`. If so, tell me and I'll remove it from the event and the model (`NewOrder`, `Order`, validation and request parsing) and update the tests and the README/`CLAUDE.md` examples. Removing a field is also a breaking schema change, so I'd raise `schemaVersion` from 3 to 4.\n\nFor the `POST /orders` request in either case, I'd keep accepting a `channel` field and ignore it rather than reject it, so existing callers don't start getting 400s.\n\nWhich option do you want? If it's option 2, how did you confirm the consumers don't read the field?",
